1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,293
They built a fire so large,

2
00:00:02,343 --> 00:00:05,846
the birds that flew over it fell from the sky.

3
00:00:05,896 --> 00:00:08,481
And into it, they threw one man...

4
00:00:08,531 --> 00:00:10,142
for the crime of saying:

5
00:00:10,192 --> 00:00:12,013
my Lord is Allah.

6
00:00:12,154 --> 00:00:13,172
But Allah said:

7
00:00:13,222 --> 00:00:17,225
"O fire, be coolness and safety upon Ibrahim."

8
00:00:17,738 --> 00:00:21,206
Who was this man, who stood alone against his father,

9
00:00:21,256 --> 00:00:23,321
his people, and a king?

10
00:00:23,404 --> 00:00:26,593
The man Allah Himself took as a friend.

11
00:00:26,643 --> 00:00:28,300
The father of the prophets.

12
00:00:28,350 --> 00:00:30,322
The one who built the Kaaba.

13
00:00:30,405 --> 00:00:36,127
This is the complete story of Prophet Ibrahim, alayhis salaam, from the Quran.

14
00:00:36,337 --> 00:00:37,798
The Friend of Allah.

15
00:00:38,800 --> 00:00:42,059
Long ago, in a land of temples and statues,

16
00:00:42,109 --> 00:00:45,066
a boy grew up surrounded by idols.

17
00:00:45,116 --> 00:00:48,259
His people bowed to statues of stone and wood.

18
00:00:48,309 --> 00:00:49,733
They brought them food.

19
00:00:49,783 --> 00:00:53,659
They begged them for rain, for children, for wealth.

20
00:00:53,800 --> 00:00:57,049
And his own father, Azar, worshipped them too.

21
00:00:57,259 --> 00:01:01,565
But the boy looked at the idols, and saw what they were:

22
00:01:01,648 --> 00:01:06,012
stone that could not hear, wood that could not see.

23
00:01:06,315 --> 00:01:08,494
One day he said to his father:

24
00:01:08,544 --> 00:01:11,083
"Do you take idols as gods?

25
00:01:11,133 --> 00:01:14,824
Indeed, I see you and your people in clear error."

26
00:01:14,965 --> 00:01:17,204
It was a dangerous thing to say.

27
00:01:17,287 --> 00:01:20,511
In that land, the idols were not only worship.

28
00:01:20,561 --> 00:01:24,588
They were power, and trade, and the honour of every family.

29
00:01:24,798 --> 00:01:29,092
But Allah had given this young man something no one around him had:

30
00:01:29,303 --> 00:01:34,177
sound judgement, and a heart that would not lie to itself.

31
00:01:35,180 --> 00:01:37,522
His people also worshipped the sky:

32
00:01:37,572 --> 00:01:40,728
the stars, the moon, the sun.

33
00:01:40,939 --> 00:01:45,858
So Ibrahim, alayhis salaam, showed them, step by step,

34
00:01:45,908 --> 00:01:48,762
why none of these could be a god.

35
00:01:48,845 --> 00:01:52,034
When the night grew dark, he saw a star, and said:

36
00:01:52,084 --> 00:01:53,903
this is my lord.

37
00:01:53,953 --> 00:01:55,948
But when it set, he said:

38
00:01:56,031 --> 00:01:58,769
"I do not love those that disappear."

39
00:01:58,887 --> 00:02:02,972
Then he saw the moon rising, bright and full, and said:

40
00:02:03,032 --> 00:02:04,712
this is my lord.

41
00:02:04,762 --> 00:02:06,523
But when it set, he said:

42
00:02:06,573 --> 00:02:08,543
unless my Lord guides me,

43
00:02:08,593 --> 00:02:11,888
I will surely be among those who go astray.

44
00:02:12,018 --> 00:02:15,627
Then the sun rose, the greatest light of all.

45
00:02:15,698 --> 00:02:19,087
This is my lord, he said, this is greater.

46
00:02:19,170 --> 00:02:23,208
But when the sun set too, he turned to his people and said:

47
00:02:23,349 --> 00:02:28,409
O my people, I am free from all that you associate with Allah.

48
00:02:28,620 --> 00:02:33,923
"Indeed, I have turned my face toward He who created the heavens and the earth,

49
00:02:33,973 --> 00:02:35,966
inclining toward truth,

50
00:02:36,016 --> 00:02:39,811
and I am not of those who associate others with Allah."

51
00:02:40,207 --> 00:02:43,013
Everything that rises... sets.

52
00:02:43,063 --> 00:02:46,637
Only the One who made them never disappears.

53
00:02:47,640 --> 00:02:52,176
The hardest person to call to Allah was the one he loved most:

54
00:02:52,226 --> 00:02:53,710
his own father.

55
00:02:53,793 --> 00:02:56,206
And listen to how gently he spoke.

56
00:02:56,289 --> 00:03:00,616
"O my father, why do you worship that which does not hear,

57
00:03:00,666 --> 00:03:04,821
and does not see, and will not benefit you at all?"

58
00:03:05,032 --> 00:03:06,143
O my father,

59
00:03:06,193 --> 00:03:09,370
knowledge has come to me that has not come to you.

60
00:03:09,420 --> 00:03:12,925
So follow me, and I will guide you to an even path.

61
00:03:13,066 --> 00:03:13,887
O my father,

62
00:03:13,937 --> 00:03:17,869
I fear that a punishment from the Most Merciful will touch you.

63
00:03:17,919 --> 00:03:19,100
Four times he said:

64
00:03:19,150 --> 00:03:20,460
O my father.

65
00:03:20,601 --> 00:03:22,886
Not once did he raise his voice.

66
00:03:22,969 --> 00:03:24,486
But his father answered:

67
00:03:24,536 --> 00:03:27,714
"Have you no desire for my gods, O Ibrahim?

68
00:03:27,764 --> 00:03:30,756
If you do not stop, I will surely stone you.

69
00:03:30,806 --> 00:03:33,509
So leave me, for a long time."

70
00:03:33,650 --> 00:03:36,746
And Ibrahim, alayhis salaam, said:

71
00:03:36,796 --> 00:03:38,418
"Peace be upon you.

72
00:03:38,468 --> 00:03:41,065
I will ask forgiveness for you from my Lord.

73
00:03:41,115 --> 00:03:44,213
Indeed, He is ever gracious to me."

74
00:03:45,260 --> 00:03:47,114
Words had not moved them.

75
00:03:47,164 --> 00:03:51,411
So Ibrahim, alayhis salaam, made a plan.

76
00:03:51,494 --> 00:03:52,872
He asked his people:

77
00:03:52,922 --> 00:03:57,492
"What are these statues to which you are devoted?" They said:

78
00:03:57,542 --> 00:04:00,478
we found our fathers worshipping them.

79
00:04:00,619 --> 00:04:01,685
He said:

80
00:04:01,768 --> 00:04:05,110
you and your fathers have been in clear error.

81
00:04:05,193 --> 00:04:06,397
And he swore:

82
00:04:06,447 --> 00:04:10,973
by Allah, I will plan against your idols after you turn your backs.

83
00:04:11,114 --> 00:04:14,315
On a festival day, the whole town left.

84
00:04:14,365 --> 00:04:16,219
The temple stood empty.

85
00:04:16,269 --> 00:04:21,027
And Ibrahim, alayhis salaam, went in alone.

86
00:04:21,168 --> 00:04:24,357
He broke the idols into pieces, all of them...

87
00:04:24,407 --> 00:04:26,148
except the biggest one.

88
00:04:26,451 --> 00:04:29,083
When the people returned, they cried:

89
00:04:29,133 --> 00:04:32,845
who has done this to our gods? Some said:

90
00:04:32,895 --> 00:04:35,051
we heard a young man speak of them.

91
00:04:35,101 --> 00:04:36,991
His name is Ibrahim.

92
00:04:37,074 --> 00:04:39,567
They brought him before everyone and asked:

93
00:04:39,617 --> 00:04:42,913
did you do this to our gods, O Ibrahim?

94
00:04:42,996 --> 00:04:43,689
He said:

95
00:04:43,739 --> 00:04:46,998
"Rather, this one, the biggest of them, did it.

96
00:04:47,048 --> 00:04:49,739
So ask them, if they can speak."

97
00:04:50,136 --> 00:04:53,118
For a moment, they looked at each other, and knew.

98
00:04:53,201 --> 00:04:55,765
Then they lowered their heads and said:

99
00:04:55,976 --> 00:04:59,015
you know very well that these do not speak.

100
00:04:59,099 --> 00:05:00,059
And he said:

101
00:05:00,109 --> 00:05:02,868
then do you worship, instead of Allah,

102
00:05:02,918 --> 00:05:05,748
what can neither benefit you nor harm you?

103
00:05:05,798 --> 00:05:08,605
Shame on you, and on what you worship.

104
00:05:08,746 --> 00:05:10,916
Will you not use reason?

105
00:05:11,920 --> 00:05:14,101
They had lost the argument.

106
00:05:14,312 --> 00:05:16,527
So they turned to force.

107
00:05:16,668 --> 00:05:20,626
"Burn him, and support your gods, if you are to act."

108
00:05:20,767 --> 00:05:22,807
They gathered wood for days.

109
00:05:22,857 --> 00:05:26,127
They built a fire so great that no one could come near it,

110
00:05:26,177 --> 00:05:29,182
and they hurled him into it from far away.

111
00:05:29,393 --> 00:05:33,012
A young man, alone, falling into the flames.

112
00:05:33,062 --> 00:05:36,216
And then Allah gave the fire a single command:

113
00:05:36,266 --> 00:05:40,757
"O fire, be coolness and safety upon Ibrahim."

114
00:05:40,898 --> 00:05:43,217
The fire that was made to burn...

115
00:05:43,267 --> 00:05:44,947
obeyed its Creator.

116
00:05:44,997 --> 00:05:47,280
It burned his ropes, and not him.

117
00:05:47,330 --> 00:05:52,123
"And they intended for him harm, but We made them the greatest losers."

118
00:05:52,264 --> 00:05:54,734
But the fire was not his hardest test.

119
00:05:54,784 --> 00:05:56,998
That one would come years later...

120
00:05:57,048 --> 00:05:58,381
in a dream.

121
00:05:59,380 --> 00:06:02,732
News of the young man in the fire reached the king.

122
00:06:02,782 --> 00:06:07,155
He was a man so proud of his kingdom that he argued with Ibrahim,

123
00:06:07,205 --> 00:06:10,745
alayhis salaam, about his Lord.

124
00:06:10,828 --> 00:06:14,052
Ibrahim, alayhis salaam, said:

125
00:06:14,102 --> 00:06:18,698
my Lord is the One who gives life and causes death.

126
00:06:18,781 --> 00:06:19,845
The king said:

127
00:06:19,895 --> 00:06:22,167
I give life and cause death.

128
00:06:22,217 --> 00:06:25,339
I can pardon a man, or have him killed.

129
00:06:25,549 --> 00:06:29,007
So Ibrahim, alayhis salaam, said:

130
00:06:29,090 --> 00:06:32,662
"Indeed, Allah brings up the sun from the east,

131
00:06:32,712 --> 00:06:35,323
so bring it up from the west."

132
00:06:35,835 --> 00:06:38,771
And the disbeliever was left speechless.

133
00:06:38,854 --> 00:06:40,975
A king, with all his armies...

134
00:06:41,025 --> 00:06:43,531
silenced by one sentence.

135
00:06:44,530 --> 00:06:46,767
His father had rejected him.

136
00:06:46,817 --> 00:06:49,147
His people had tried to burn him.

137
00:06:49,197 --> 00:06:51,622
His king had become his enemy.

138
00:06:51,833 --> 00:06:53,989
Only a few believed in him.

139
00:06:54,039 --> 00:06:58,470
Among them was his nephew, Lut, alayhis salaam.

140
00:06:58,520 --> 00:07:03,311
So Ibrahim, alayhis salaam, left the land of his birth,

141
00:07:03,361 --> 00:07:05,622
with nothing but his faith.

142
00:07:05,672 --> 00:07:06,412
He said:

143
00:07:06,462 --> 00:07:08,804
"Indeed, I will go to my Lord.

144
00:07:08,854 --> 00:07:10,362
He will guide me."

145
00:07:10,503 --> 00:07:14,481
He travelled for years, through deserts and foreign lands,

146
00:07:14,531 --> 00:07:17,745
calling people to Allah wherever he went.

147
00:07:17,829 --> 00:07:21,180
And as he grew older, he made one more dua:

148
00:07:21,230 --> 00:07:25,314
"My Lord, grant me a child from among the righteous."

149
00:07:25,364 --> 00:07:27,264
And Allah gave him good news:

150
00:07:27,314 --> 00:07:29,042
a forbearing boy.

151
00:07:30,040 --> 00:07:33,811
His son Ismail, alayhis salaam, was born.

152
00:07:33,953 --> 00:07:37,109
And then came a test that no father would choose.

153
00:07:37,250 --> 00:07:43,713
By Allah's command, Ibrahim, alayhis salaam, brought the baby and his mother to a dry valley,

154
00:07:43,763 --> 00:07:47,117
with no water, no plants, and no people.

155
00:07:47,200 --> 00:07:49,114
The valley of Makkah.

156
00:07:49,197 --> 00:07:50,169
He left them there,

157
00:07:50,219 --> 00:07:53,526
with a bag of dates and a skin of water.

158
00:07:53,655 --> 00:07:56,542
As he walked away, the mother called after him:

159
00:07:56,592 --> 00:08:00,666
has Allah commanded you to do this? He said: yes.

160
00:08:00,737 --> 00:08:01,628
And she said:

161
00:08:01,678 --> 00:08:04,056
then He will not abandon us.

162
00:08:04,255 --> 00:08:08,873
And Ibrahim, alayhis salaam, turned to the sky and prayed:

163
00:08:08,957 --> 00:08:16,105
"Our Lord, I have settled some of my descendants in an uncultivated valley near Your sacred House,

164
00:08:16,155 --> 00:08:18,405
that they may establish prayer."

165
00:08:18,616 --> 00:08:22,537
When the water ran out, the mother ran between two hills,

166
00:08:22,587 --> 00:08:27,693
Safa and Marwa, seven times, searching for any sign of help.

167
00:08:27,823 --> 00:08:31,687
And at the baby's feet, water burst from the ground.

168
00:08:31,886 --> 00:08:34,181
The spring of Zamzam.

169
00:08:34,231 --> 00:08:36,236
It is still flowing today.

170
00:08:36,286 --> 00:08:40,068
Every pilgrim who walks between Safa and Marwa is

171
00:08:40,118 --> 00:08:43,576
walking in the footsteps of a mother who trusted Allah.

172
00:08:43,717 --> 00:08:45,805
And that baby would grow up...

173
00:08:45,888 --> 00:08:48,870
to become the son in his father's dream.

174
00:08:49,870 --> 00:08:54,559
Ibrahim, alayhis salaam, had seen the fire turn cool.

175
00:08:54,642 --> 00:08:57,146
He had seen water rise from a desert.

176
00:08:57,196 --> 00:09:01,176
And still, he asked his Lord for one more thing.

177
00:09:01,480 --> 00:09:04,808
"My Lord, show me how You give life to the dead."

178
00:09:04,858 --> 00:09:05,853
Allah said:

179
00:09:05,903 --> 00:09:07,687
have you not believed? He said:

180
00:09:07,737 --> 00:09:11,403
"Yes, but only that my heart may be satisfied."

181
00:09:11,453 --> 00:09:16,186
So Allah told him to take four birds, cut them into pieces,

182
00:09:16,236 --> 00:09:18,684
and put a part of them on each hill.

183
00:09:19,080 --> 00:09:20,551
Then call them.

184
00:09:20,601 --> 00:09:21,643
He called...

185
00:09:21,693 --> 00:09:25,708
and they came flying back to him, alive, in haste.

186
00:09:25,849 --> 00:09:28,272
Faith does not mean you never ask.

187
00:09:28,322 --> 00:09:31,699
It means you ask the One who has the answer.

188
00:09:32,700 --> 00:09:33,985
Years passed.

189
00:09:34,035 --> 00:09:36,435
Ismail, alayhis salaam,

190
00:09:36,485 --> 00:09:40,709
grew into a boy who could walk and work beside his father.

191
00:09:40,920 --> 00:09:44,982
Then Ibrahim, alayhis salaam, saw a dream.

192
00:09:45,123 --> 00:09:48,346
And the dreams of prophets are revelation.

193
00:09:48,396 --> 00:09:49,194
He said:

194
00:09:49,244 --> 00:09:50,540
"O my son,

195
00:09:50,590 --> 00:09:54,325
indeed I have seen in a dream that I sacrifice you.

196
00:09:54,375 --> 00:09:56,090
So see what you think."

197
00:09:56,140 --> 00:09:57,564
And the boy answered:

198
00:09:57,614 --> 00:10:00,536
"O my father, do as you are commanded.

199
00:10:00,586 --> 00:10:04,067
You will find me, if Allah wills, of the patient."

200
00:10:04,209 --> 00:10:06,818
When they had both submitted, and Ibrahim,

201
00:10:06,868 --> 00:10:10,986
alayhis salaam, laid him down on his forehead...

202
00:10:11,036 --> 00:10:12,820
Allah called to him:

203
00:10:12,870 --> 00:10:16,305
O Ibrahim, you have fulfilled the vision.

204
00:10:16,388 --> 00:10:19,393
Indeed, this was the clear trial.

205
00:10:19,476 --> 00:10:23,108
"And We ransomed him with a great sacrifice."

206
00:10:23,412 --> 00:10:28,716
Every Eid al-Adha, Muslims around the world remember this moment:

207
00:10:28,799 --> 00:10:33,337
a father and a son who loved Allah more than anything.

208
00:10:34,340 --> 00:10:38,179
Ibrahim, alayhis salaam, was now an old man.

209
00:10:38,229 --> 00:10:42,024
And his wife, Sarah, had never had a child.

210
00:10:42,142 --> 00:10:44,681
One day, guests arrived at his tent.

211
00:10:44,731 --> 00:10:49,930
Strangers, whom no one knew. They said: peace. He said: peace.

212
00:10:50,048 --> 00:10:55,211
Ibrahim, alayhis salaam, was known for his generosity.

213
00:10:55,261 --> 00:10:57,753
Without a word, he went to his family,

214
00:10:57,803 --> 00:11:01,354
and came back with a fat roasted calf.

215
00:11:01,495 --> 00:11:03,453
He placed it near them and said:

216
00:11:03,503 --> 00:11:07,610
"Will you not eat?" But their hands did not reach for it.

217
00:11:07,660 --> 00:11:09,481
And he felt afraid of them.

218
00:11:09,622 --> 00:11:10,118
They said:

219
00:11:10,168 --> 00:11:11,721
do not fear.

220
00:11:11,863 --> 00:11:15,237
We are messengers, sent to the people of Lut.

221
00:11:15,287 --> 00:11:17,687
And they gave him good news.

222
00:11:17,737 --> 00:11:21,007
His wife, who was standing nearby, smiled.

223
00:11:21,057 --> 00:11:23,213
And they gave her the good news of a son,

224
00:11:23,263 --> 00:11:28,114
Ishaq, and after Ishaq, Yaqub, alayhimus salaam.

225
00:11:28,255 --> 00:11:29,099
She said:

226
00:11:29,149 --> 00:11:31,491
shall I give birth, when I am an old woman,

227
00:11:31,541 --> 00:11:34,021
and my husband is an old man?

228
00:11:34,071 --> 00:11:37,400
This is an amazing thing! They said:

229
00:11:37,450 --> 00:11:40,453
"Are you amazed at the decree of Allah?

230
00:11:40,503 --> 00:11:44,192
May the mercy of Allah and His blessings be upon you,

231
00:11:44,242 --> 00:11:45,877
people of the house."

232
00:11:46,018 --> 00:11:52,471
From Ismail, alayhis salaam, would come the Prophet Muhammad, peace be upon him.

233
00:11:52,554 --> 00:11:56,278
From Ishaq, alayhis salaam, would come Yaqub,

234
00:11:56,328 --> 00:12:02,328
Yusuf, Musa, Dawud, Sulaiman and Isa, alayhimus salaam.

235
00:12:02,411 --> 00:12:04,569
The father of the prophets.

236
00:12:05,570 --> 00:12:10,129
Then Allah showed Ibrahim, alayhis salaam, the place of His House.

237
00:12:10,179 --> 00:12:13,300
And father and son began to build.

238
00:12:13,418 --> 00:12:17,304
Ibrahim, alayhis salaam, laid the stones.

239
00:12:17,354 --> 00:12:20,508
Ismail, alayhis salaam, carried them.

240
00:12:20,558 --> 00:12:24,167
And as the walls of the Kaaba rose, they prayed:

241
00:12:24,239 --> 00:12:26,882
"Our Lord, accept this from us.

242
00:12:26,932 --> 00:12:30,274
Indeed, You are the Hearing, the Knowing."

243
00:12:30,554 --> 00:12:33,093
Our Lord, make us Muslims to You,

244
00:12:33,143 --> 00:12:36,079
and from our descendants a Muslim nation.

245
00:12:36,162 --> 00:12:39,759
Show us our rites, and accept our repentance.

246
00:12:40,063 --> 00:12:42,430
And they asked for one more thing:

247
00:12:42,571 --> 00:12:46,027
our Lord, send among them a messenger from themselves,

248
00:12:46,077 --> 00:12:48,502
who will recite Your verses to them.

249
00:12:48,643 --> 00:12:51,983
Thousands of years later, that dua was answered:

250
00:12:52,033 --> 00:12:55,735
Prophet Muhammad, peace be upon him.

251
00:12:55,806 --> 00:12:57,556
Then Allah commanded:

252
00:12:57,606 --> 00:13:00,238
"Proclaim to the people the Hajj.

253
00:13:00,288 --> 00:13:02,304
They will come to you on foot,

254
00:13:02,354 --> 00:13:06,427
and on every lean camel, from every distant pass."

255
00:13:06,569 --> 00:13:08,065
And they still come.

256
00:13:08,276 --> 00:13:14,021
Millions of people every year, answering the call of Ibrahim, alayhis salaam.

257
00:13:15,020 --> 00:13:21,007
In his old age, Ibrahim, alayhis salaam, stood in the valley that had once been empty,

258
00:13:21,057 --> 00:13:25,723
and he made a dua that Muslims still recite today.

259
00:13:25,853 --> 00:13:28,752
"My Lord, make this city secure,

260
00:13:28,802 --> 00:13:32,933
and keep me and my sons away from worshipping idols."

261
00:13:33,005 --> 00:13:34,661
Praise be to Allah,

262
00:13:34,711 --> 00:13:38,970
who gave me in my old age Ismail and Ishaq.

263
00:13:39,088 --> 00:13:41,977
Indeed, my Lord hears every prayer.

264
00:13:42,037 --> 00:13:47,388
"My Lord, make me one who establishes prayer, and from my descendants too.

265
00:13:47,505 --> 00:13:50,242
Our Lord, and accept my dua."

266
00:13:50,292 --> 00:13:53,179
"Our Lord, forgive me, and my parents,

267
00:13:53,229 --> 00:13:57,244
and the believers, on the Day the account is established."

268
00:13:57,455 --> 00:14:00,052
Many of us say this dua in every prayer,

269
00:14:00,102 --> 00:14:02,155
at the end of our salah.

270
00:14:02,296 --> 00:14:05,787
The words of Ibrahim, alayhis salaam,

271
00:14:05,837 --> 00:14:09,922
still on our tongues, thousands of years later.

272
00:14:10,920 --> 00:14:13,900
A boy among idols who would not bow.

273
00:14:13,950 --> 00:14:17,838
A son who spoke gently to a father who threatened him.

274
00:14:17,921 --> 00:14:19,995
A young man in the fire.

275
00:14:20,045 --> 00:14:22,317
A father in a dry valley.

276
00:14:22,367 --> 00:14:27,089
An old man laying stones for a House he would never see filled.

277
00:14:27,139 --> 00:14:29,109
Every time, he was alone.

278
00:14:29,159 --> 00:14:31,990
And every time, Allah was enough for him.

279
00:14:32,108 --> 00:14:33,488
Allah says:

280
00:14:33,548 --> 00:14:37,830
"There has already been for you an excellent example in Ibrahim."

281
00:14:37,948 --> 00:14:40,988
And Allah left his name in our prayers.

282
00:14:41,245 --> 00:14:42,530
Every time we pray,

283
00:14:42,580 --> 00:14:47,093
we send blessings on Ibrahim and the family of Ibrahim.

284
00:14:47,143 --> 00:14:49,532
"Peace upon Ibrahim."

285
00:14:49,582 --> 00:14:50,878
So when you feel alone,

286
00:14:50,928 --> 00:14:54,094
say what he said as they threw him into the fire:

287
00:14:54,144 --> 00:14:57,532
Hasbunallahu wa ni'mal wakeel.

288
00:14:57,674 --> 00:15:01,538
Allah is enough for us, and He is the best Guardian.

289
00:15:01,609 --> 00:15:04,614
Which moment of his story moved you most?

290
00:15:04,686 --> 00:15:06,366
Tell us in the comments.

291
00:15:06,416 --> 00:15:08,490
Subscribe to Haq Stories,

292
00:15:08,540 --> 00:15:13,939
and watch the complete story of Prophet Musa, alayhis salaam, next.
